# .gitignore for DbDo, generated by homerTidy on 2026-09-19.
#
# THIS IS A WHITELIST. Everything is ignored, and then exactly what
# RepoFiles.txt names is put back. A file dropped into this folder is
# invisible to git until somebody names it there.
#
# To add a file, add one line to RepoFiles.txt and run homerTidy --gitignore.

# Ignore everything.
/*

# Put back what the project names.
!/.gitignore
!/2db.cs
!/accept.inix
!/buildDbDo.cmd
!/DbDo.cs
!/DbDo.exe.config
!/DbDo.ico
!/DbDo.inix
!/DbDo.js
!/DbDo.manifest
!/DbDo.nvda-addon
!/DbDo_hotkeys.inix
!/DbDo_JAWS.zip
!/DbDo_setup.iss
!/help/
!/License.htm
!/License.md
!/ReadMe.htm
!/ReadMe.md
!/RepoFiles.txt
!/uiTest.inix
!/version.txt

# Never pushed, whatever RepoFiles.txt says.
*.exe
*.log
*.obj
*.pdb
.venv/
build/
create*Repo.cmd
create*Repo.ps1
dist/
notes/
self.htm
self.md
tagRelease.cmd
tagRelease.ps1
Version.cs
__pycache__/
version.py

# FETCHED, NOT AUTHORED. buildTutorials downloads about 86 MB of voice engine
# and voice model into scripts/voices, and speaks the tutorials into help as
# .mp3 and .mkv. None of it is source: it is rebuilt by one command, it is far
# larger than everything else here put together, and a zip of the folder with it
# in is 80 MB of the wrong thing.
scripts/voices/
scripts/ffmpeg.exe
help/Tutorial_*.inix
help/*.mp3
help/*.wav
help/Tutorials.m3u
